    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<h2>Scavenger Savant</h2><p><em>Every ruin is a pantry if you know where to pry.</em></p><hr /><h3>Rules</h3><p>You gain a skill rank in Investigation (Mind). If you already have it, you gain mastery.</p><p>When you spend at least 10 minutes searching a wreck, ruin, or battlefield, you may declare what you are looking for (ammo, medicine, parts, food, trade goods). You then make an Investigation (Mind) check. On a success (DC set by the GM), you find something relevant and useful; on a failure, you still find something, but it comes with a complication (noise, contamination, time loss, or unwanted attention).</p>",
